  "description": "Dodo (no, not the bird) is the Nigerian name for sweet, fried ripe plantains eaten in or alongside savory dishes, not dessert.",
  "notes": "Notes: In Step 2, you can add 3/4 teaspoon to 1 teaspoon of a spice blend (like pumpkin spice or apple spice) or a combination of ground cayenne pepper, ground ginger, ground cinnamon, and ground cloves.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Fried plantains are best enjoyed immediately, though leftovers can be refrigerated in an airtight container overnight; reheat in the microwave, in a skillet with oil, or in a moderate oven.",
